      },
      "displayName": "Former user",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>On the Fedora side the following happens:<br/>\nFedoraClient.getAPIM() calls FedoraClient.getSOAPStub() which calls APIAStubFactory.getStubAltPath(). Here a check Administrator.INSTANCE == null occurs which initializes the static variables of the Administrator class. Some of them happen to be AWT based, so X (or headless) is needed which can clearly be seen by the \"focus stealing\" effect on OSX.</p>\n",
     "created": "16/Dec/09 8:21 AM",
     "id": "11169",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10572/comment/11169",
